      },
      "statement": "Kyverno 1.13 removes the wildcard view permission that previously allowed Kyverno controllers to view all resources including secrets and adds a role binding to the default `view` role instead; policies during admission controls are unaffected, but reports may be impacted and the controller may no longer be able to view custom resources used by mutate and generate policies."
    },
    "corrected": {
      "applicability": {
        "exposure": {
          "op": "all",
          "of": [
            {
              "op": "any",
              "of": [
                {
                  "op": "gvk-in-use",
                  "group": "kyverno.io",
                  "kind": "ClusterPolicy"
                },
                {
                  "op": "gvk-in-use",
                  "group": "kyverno.io",
                  "kind": "Policy"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "op": "undecidable",
              "reason": "evidence-gap",
              "needed": "which resources (e.g. custom resources) the environment's reports or mutate/generate policies need to view that the default Kubernetes view role does not grant to the Kyverno controllers"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "statement": "Kyverno 1.13 removes the controllers' wildcard view permission and binds them to the default `view` role. Exposed: environments using ClusterPolicy or Policy whose reports, or whose mutate/generate policies, need to view resources (e.g. custom resources) the default view role does not grant. Admission-time policy evaluation is unaffected."
    },
